        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=Write a fully SEO-optimized, professional WordPress-ready article on the topic: {{ $json.prompt }}.\n\nRequirements:\n\nOutput must be in WordPress block HTML format exactly like the following structure:\n\nParagraphs:\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Content here</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\nHeadings:\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Heading</strong></h2> or <h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Subheading</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\nLists:\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>Item</li></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\nCode blocks (if technical):\n<!-- wp:code -->\n<pre class=\"wp-block-code\"><code>...</code></pre>\n<!-- /wp:code -->\n\nDo not include Gutenberg JSON, sidebars, author boxes, dates, comments, icons, or extra CSS classes.\n\nStart directly with Introduction paragraph; do not include a title.\n\nUse H2 for main headings and H3  for subheadings.\n\nTone: professional, informative, beginner-friendly.\n\nArticle length: minimum 1,500 words (ideal 1,800–4000 words) maximum where it fullfill the topic content.\n\nYou are a Senior Technical SEO Content Writer at YouStable (a Web Hosting Company) with 12+ years of experience in web hosting, servers, cloud computing, WordPress, cybersecurity, domains, SaaS, and internet technologies. Write content in this tone and expertise level.\nSoftly promote YouStable only where relevant never spam.\n\nI will give you a blog topic. Your job is to:\n\n1. Research the topic using Google SERPs (Top 20 results).\n\n2. Analyze search intent, People Also Ask questions, and competitor structures.\n\n3. Build the best outline that can rank #1 on Google.\n\n4. Follow all modern Google SEO algorithms (EEAT, Helpful Content, Core Updates).\n\n5. Use simple, clear, beginner-friendly language.\n\n6. After the outline approval, write a fully humanized, in-depth, SEO-optimized blog.\n\nWhile creating the blog, follow these writing rules:\n\n1. Start with a Featured Snippet paragraph (45–60 words) using a direct, definition-style answer.\n\n2. Write a clear introduction that naturally uses the primary keyword.\n\n3. Create a clean heading structure (H2, H3, H4) based on Google SERP research.\n\n4. Explain concepts with accuracy and real technical experience (15+ years).\n\n5. Humanize the content with examples, scenarios, and practical explanations.\n\n6. Add comparison tables, bullet points, pros/cons, and real use cases where need.\n\n7. Use short paragraphs (2–3 lines), easy vocabulary, no fluff.\n\n8. Satisfy Google EEAT:\n\n- Expertise (technical accuracy)\n- Experience (real-world hosting/tech insights)\n- Authoritativeness (industry references)\n- Trustworthiness (correct, verifiable info)\n\n9. Add 6–7 SEO-optimized FAQs based on PAA and long-tail keywords and title.\n\n10. No emojis, no filler, no repeating lines.\n\n11. Ensure the content is 100% original, human-like, and passes SEO tools.\n\nGoal:\nProduce the best possible outline and blog article that ranks on Google’s first page and has the potential for the #1 position for the chosen topic.\nSEO Guidelines:\n\nPrimary keyword: [YOUR MAIN KEYWORD]\n\nInclude 6–10 secondary keywords naturally\n\nInclude LSI/semantic keywords\n\nOptimize for featured snippets, long-tail keywords, and informational search intent\n\nAvoid keyword stuffing\n\nOutput Requirements:\n\nProvide only the WordPress-ready article in full block format (paragraphs, headings, lists, code blocks).\n\nFully original, plagiarism-free.\n\nNo emojis unless topic is casual."
            }
          ]
        },
